qlitehtml: add a QPixmap provider for document images.

load_image() currently always asks the data callback for bytes and decodes
them with QPixmap::loadFromData(). Hosts that already hold decoded pixmaps
(e.g. Markdown formula/diagram images generated as QImages) pay an
unnecessary PNG/base64 round trip on every setDocument().

Let the host install a pixmap callback. It is consulted before the data
callback; a null pixmap falls back to the existing byte path. The callback
is copied into the temporary container used by print(), so token-based
images survive PDF export.

Images served by the callback are static: loadAnimation() is skipped by
design. Animated images must keep using the data callback.

